From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:46:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: ct709: check the auxiliary gain before sampling

The fixed 16x capture uses gain index 4, which requires AUX=0 as well as GAIN=2. Reject unsupported auxiliary settings before writing to the device and allow the caller to sample again when the setting changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
---
 drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.c | 2 ++
 drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.h | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.c b/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.c
index 1bbb372ee..d3172c467 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.c
@@ -99,6 +99,8 @@ static int ct709_read_raw(struct iio_dev *indio,
 	}
 	d->deadline = ktime_get_ns() + 5ULL * NSEC_PER_SEC;
 	ret = als_once(&ct709_ops, d, &result);
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && !result.changed)
+		goto out;
 	if (ret || !result.valid || !result.restored) {
 		d->faulted = true;
 		if (!ret)
diff --git a/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.h b/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.h
index 7f26a62ab..9e9fb24ff 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.h
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/ams-ct709.h
@@ -89,6 +89,14 @@ static int als_once(const struct als_ops *o, void *ctx, struct als_result *r)
 		ret = -EPERM;
 		goto finish;
 	}
+	/* GAIN=2 gives the advertised 16x range only with AUX gain disabled. */
+	ret = als_read(o, ctx, 0x90, &v);
+	if (ret)
+		goto finish;
+	if (v != 0) {
+		ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		goto finish;
+	}
 	/*
 	 * Configure only after exact original admission; any write can be
 	 * ambiguous.
